insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('01d5406e-1c96-59ca-8493-66507ea82909', 'rg5-context-clues-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Hill on Mile Two$q$, $q$Hana Kim had joined the cross-country team in September. Her first race was on a muddy course through a park. Before the start, Coach Bello gave her some advice. "Don't sprint at the beginning," he said. "Save your energy for the hill on mile two."

When the whistle blew, many runners dashed ahead. Hana kept a steady pace. By the time she reached the hill, she could see that several of the fast starters were fatigued. They were breathing hard, and their legs looked heavy.

The hill was steep and slippery. Hana leaned forward and took short steps. She did not stop, even when her legs burned. Slowly, she passed one runner, then another.

At the top, she felt exhausted, but she kept going. Near the finish line, her teammates were cheering. Their encouragement gave her a boost of energy, and she raced the last stretch.

Hana finished in twelfth place. It was not first, but Coach Bello said her plan had been wise. Hana agreed. Next time, she wanted to do even better.$q$, 'draft')
