   $q$Which quotation best supports the idea that glaciers can carry heavy objects a long way?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Most glaciers move only a few inches or feet each day.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"Sometimes a single boulder ends up sitting alone in a field, far from any rock like it.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"They leave long scratches on the bedrock below.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"\"Over time, the bottom layers turn into thick, solid ice.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Sometimes a single boulder ends up sitting alone in a field, far from any rock like it."$q$, $q$A boulder left "far from any rock like it" shows the ice moved it a long distance. The scratches show rocks dragging along the ground, but not how far anything was carried.$q$, 'draft', '9bd03cc1-2186-54a1-b9a6-fc9ce87d99ca')
