   $q$What can the reader infer about why a main cable is made of thousands of wires instead of one thick piece?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is safer, because the cable still holds if a few wires wear out.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is lighter, because thin wires have no weight to carry at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It is cheaper, because thin wires cost nothing to make or replace.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It is quicker, because crews never have to check the cable again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is safer, because the cable still holds if a few wires wear out.$q$, $q$The passage says, "If a few wires wear out, the others still share the load," which shows the design keeps the bridge safe. It also says crews "check the cables often," so the choice about never checking the cable again goes against the text.$q$, 'draft', '290c9b49-2cf4-5706-8df6-56df663afd45')
