   $q$A reader claims, "Only people who cannot walk play wheelchair basketball." Which quotation best shows that this claim is not accurate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"The big difference is that every player moves in a sport wheelchair.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-wrong-claim"},{"text":"\"The sport has grown over the years.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"\"Today, teams play in schools, colleges and community leagues.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"\"Some teams include players who can walk but have injuries to their knees or ankles.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Some teams include players who can walk but have injuries to their knees or ankles."$q$, $q$The passage directly says some players "can walk," which shows the claim is wrong. The sentence that every player uses a wheelchair is true, but it says nothing about whether players can walk.$q$, 'draft', '6593489f-ceb8-561a-8b3b-e3076c9e1598')
