  ('fa7f3172-5be3-5145-9287-7e62a40a424f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The passage says paper "became much cheaper" once people made it from wood. Which two details together best explain why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Workers used a heavy press, and they stacked felts into a tall pile.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"The cloth was cut into pieces, and then it was beaten into tiny fibers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Paper was made one sheet at a time, and the sheets were hung up to dry.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Paper made from rags was often hard to get, and wood was far easier to find.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Paper made from rags was often hard to get, and wood was far easier to find.$q$, $q$The last paragraph explains that rags were scarce while wood "was far easier to find," so paper cost less. The other pairs describe steps of the process and do not explain any change in price.$q$, 'draft', '6a6d670c-33e5-5154-9a57-ce09c9a1e33e')
