  ('be4e2906-def7-51e6-a2ef-537ee09773c0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$In paragraph 2, the arms "work like busy hands searching a dark closet." What does this simile show about the arms?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They stay still and rest most of the time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They feel around carefully to find things.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are used to open and shut doors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They can only work when it is dark out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They feel around carefully to find things.$q$, $q$Hands in a dark closet feel around because they cannot see, and the paragraph says the suckers can "taste as well as grip." The simile is about exploring by touch, not about closets or darkness.$q$, 'draft', 'be6f451d-b89d-521b-9668-dcbabc3d4534')
