-- Passage rg5-figurative-language-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a', 'rg5-figurative-language-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Last Hill$q$, $q$The cross-country course at Willow Creek Park was three kilometers long. Tomas Herrera had run it in practice many times, but race day felt different. The cold air nipped at his ears as he waited at the starting line.

The whistle blew, and the runners shot forward like a flock of startled pigeons. Tomas stayed near the middle of the pack. His coach had told him, "Slow and steady wins the race." He did not want to burn out too early.

By the second kilometer, Tomas had passed two runners. His breathing was even, and his legs felt strong. Then he reached the last hill. It was a giant wall of mud and roots. With every step, his legs turned to lead.

At the top, Tomas saw his teammate Kofi just ahead. Kofi looked back and grinned. "We're almost there!" he called. Tomas dug deep and found one last burst of speed.

The two friends crossed the finish line side by side. They did not win the race, but they both beat their best times. Tomas bent over, panting. His legs were tired, but his spirits were high.$q$, 'draft')
