   $q$In paragraph 2, the runners "shot forward like a flock of startled pigeons." What does this simile show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The runners flapped their arms like wings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The runners started slowly, one by one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The runners were frightened by real birds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"The runners took off quickly, all at once.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The runners took off quickly, all at once.$q$, $q$Startled pigeons burst into the air together, and the runners leave the moment "the whistle blew." No birds are in the race, so the simile is about speed and timing.$q$, 'draft', 'cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a')
