  ('206884fb-57ce-5113-83c1-6ecc4172644b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 3, "His breathing was even." Which word is an antonym of "even" as it is used in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"odd","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"quiet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"related-not-opposite"},{"text":"steady","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"synonym-not-antonym"},{"text":"ragged","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$ragged$q$, $q$Here "even" means smooth and regular, so its opposite is "ragged," meaning rough and uneven. "Odd" is the opposite of "even" only when talking about numbers, which is a different meaning.$q$, 'draft', 'cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a')
