   $q$In paragraph 1, Amara "felt like a fish out of water." What does this idiom mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She felt out of place in her new city.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She was thirsty after the long move.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She felt happy and at home right away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She wanted to go swimming in a lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She felt out of place in her new city.$q$, $q$The next sentence says the streets were loud and she "did not know a single person," so she felt uncomfortable. A fish out of water is in the wrong place, not looking for a swim.$q$, 'draft', '40ee821a-033c-5050-8a63-60585f5cb2bf')
