   $q$In paragraph 1, the sky can "change in a heartbeat." What does this idiom mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sky changes only in the summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The sky can change very quickly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The sky changes slowly over many days.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The sky changes when your heart beats.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sky can change very quickly.$q$, $q$A heartbeat takes less than a second, and the paragraph says a storm "soon" rolls in after the clouds darken. The phrase is about speed, not about anyone's heart.$q$, 'draft', '03e0eb7d-ec8f-5b7a-bb86-45fc728e4fcf')
