   $q$The word "bolt" is a homograph. In paragraph 3, what does "bolt" mean in "A bolt of lightning"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a long roll of cloth in a store","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"a sudden run away from danger","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"a metal bar that locks a door shut","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-homograph-meaning"},{"text":"a single bright streak of electricity","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a single bright streak of electricity$q$, $q$The sentences around it call lightning "a giant spark" that heats the air, so "bolt" means one streak of it. A door lock is a different meaning of the same spelling.$q$, 'draft', '03e0eb7d-ec8f-5b7a-bb86-45fc728e4fcf')
