   $q$In paragraph 3, "the air expands with a boom." Which word is an antonym of "expands"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"heats","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"booms","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"related-not-opposite"},{"text":"spreads","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"synonym-not-antonym"},{"text":"shrinks","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$shrinks$q$, $q$"Expands" means grows larger, so its opposite is "shrinks." "Spreads" means nearly the same as "expands," and "heats" is the cause of the expanding, not its opposite.$q$, 'draft', '03e0eb7d-ec8f-5b7a-bb86-45fc728e4fcf')
