   $q$Who is the speaker of this poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The city bus that drives Route Nine","is_correct":true},{"text":"The baker who rides the bus to work","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-with-character"},{"text":"The man reading a book late at night","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-with-character"},{"text":"A student riding home after school","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-with-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The city bus that drives Route Nine$q$, $q$The speaker says "My doors swing wide" and "rest my wheels," so the speaker is the bus. The baker and students are riders the bus describes, not the speaker.$q$, 'draft', '1189a38b-da30-5eac-bcdf-dc53c9245399')
