   $q$How does the last stanza fit into the structure of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It goes back to the start of the same day the poem described.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-sequence"},{"text":"It ends the poem with the bus being taken off its route.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It moves from one day to every day, showing the routine repeats.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It describes a fourth group of riders who come late at night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It moves from one day to every day, showing the routine repeats.$q$, $q$The first three stanzas cover one day, and the last says "Tomorrow" and "I'll hum and start another day," so the poem widens to show the cycle repeating. The bus promises to keep coming, not to leave its route.$q$, 'draft', '1189a38b-da30-5eac-bcdf-dc53c9245399')
