insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('800ecc9d-567a-5981-a92e-5f746fae9ff4', 'rg5-text-structure-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Paper Then and Now$q$, $q$Text A: A Short History of Paper

About two thousand years ago, people in China made the first paper from tree bark and old cloth. For hundreds of years, the method stayed a secret. Later, travelers carried the idea west along trade routes. By around the year 1100, paper mills were running in Spain. Centuries after that, machines were invented that could make paper in long rolls. Today, paper is so common that most people use it every day without thinking.

Text B: Too Much Paper at Willow Grove School

Last year, Willow Grove School had a problem. Its recycling bins were full of paper that had been used only on one side. The student council decided to find a fix. First, they set up "second side" trays in every classroom. Students could take used sheets from the trays for rough drafts and math work. The council also asked teachers to post homework online when possible. By spring, the school was throwing away about half as much paper as before.$q$, 'draft')
