   $q$Why does the author have the spider rebuild in the same spot once before she changes her plan?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the spider is lazy and does not want to climb down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"To show that repeating a failed plan does not work, which sets up her change.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain that spiders must rebuild their webs every single night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To prove that the grasshopper was right when it told her to give up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that repeating a failed plan does not work, which sets up her change.$q$, $q$The second failure makes the spider's final words about "doing the same thing" meaningful. The ending shows the grasshopper was wrong, since the spider did not give up and succeeded.$q$, 'draft', '10129b83-73e0-5e8b-80f8-384b42794b81')
