   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The fastest swimmer should always swim the last leg of a relay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Older sisters always know the right thing to say before a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Winning first place is the only way to make a team proud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Focusing on doing your own best can matter more than winning.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Focusing on doing your own best can matter more than winning.$q$, $q$Kenji focuses on "his own lane," swims his best time and feels proud even though the team finishes third. The team cheers without winning, so the idea that only first place counts is wrong.$q$, 'draft', '258f9122-b6b9-50eb-a014-594b0ffde069')
