insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9adee0c5-4154-5699-a8ec-028bf818610b', 'rg5-word-parts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$A Weather Station on the Roof$q$, $q$Last fall, the fifth graders at Willow Creek School set up a weather station on the school roof. A local weather expert came to help them choose the tools.

The most important tool was a thermometer. It measured how warm or cold the air was every hour. A second tool, the rain gauge, collected rain in a tall tube with lines marked on the side.

The best part was that the station was automatic. Nobody had to climb onto the roof to read the numbers. The station sent its readings to a classroom computer all by itself.

Each day at midday, two students checked the computer and wrote the readings on a big chart. They also took a photograph of the sky from the classroom window. Over time, the photos showed how clouds changed before a storm.

By spring, the class could see patterns. Thick gray clouds were visible in the photos about a day before most rainstorms. The students began making their own forecasts, and they were right more often than not.$q$, 'draft')
