   $q$The Latin root aud means "hear." Who was the "audience" at the library?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The people who came to listen to Mr. Delgado","is_correct":true},{"text":"The people who spoke during question time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-role"},{"text":"The characters in the Harbor Fox books","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The workers who ran the town library","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The people who came to listen to Mr. Delgado$q$, $q$An audience is a group of people who listen, and the passage says everyone grew quiet "so they could hear him." Some people asked questions, but the audience is everyone who came to listen.$q$, 'draft', 'd809b07f-e0a6-5872-8ee0-dbdba5f9beb3')
