   $q$The Latin prefix sub- means "under" or "below." What is a "subway"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A shortcut for people walking across town","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"A small road used only by wagons and carts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A bridge for trains that runs above the street","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A path for trains that runs below the ground","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A path for trains that runs below the ground$q$, $q$Sub- means "under," and the passage calls the subway "a system of tunnels below the streets." A bridge above the street is the opposite of what sub- signals.$q$, 'draft', 'dd8926fb-a5c6-5679-946e-60f15046f137')
