   $q$The Greek root geo means "earth," and graph means "write or describe." What had Mei studied when she studied "geography"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The places, lands, and waters of the earth","is_correct":true},{"text":"The way living things grow and change","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-bio-root"},{"text":"The history of her own family members","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"The way to write neat and clear letters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-geo-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The places, lands, and waters of the earth$q$, $q$Geography describes the earth, and Mei used it to know the island's name and the warm water around it. Living things would be biology, which uses the root bio.$q$, 'draft', 'f72347d9-a04c-5ee8-ad9b-7cce5b614929')
