insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('17773410-8578-588b-a135-7ef47bcf2369', 'rg5-word-parts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Listening to a Restless Mountain$q$, $q$Some mountains are not as quiet as they look. Deep below them, hot melted rock slowly moves and pushes upward. Scientists keep watch on these mountains to keep nearby towns safe.

A geologist is a scientist who studies the earth and its rocks. Geologists place special tools on the sides of a mountain. These tools measure tiny shakes in the ground that people cannot feel. They also measure gases that rise from cracks in the rock.

When the shaking grows stronger and the gases increase, geologists know that melted rock is rising. These signs help them predict when an eruption might happen. An eruption is when melted rock, ash, and gas burst out of the mountain.

Even a small eruption can disrupt daily life. Ash can cover roads, close schools, and stop airplanes from flying. Thick ash in the air is dangerous to breathe.

Thanks to early warnings, towns have time to prepare. Families pack supplies, and buses wait to carry people to safety. Careful science turns a frightening event into one that people can plan for.$q$, 'draft')
