   $q$The prefix pre- means "before," and dict means "say." What do the signs help geologists do when they "predict" an eruption?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Stop it from happening at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Measure how much ash fell on the roads","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-meter-root"},{"text":"Explain why it happened after it is over","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"Tell ahead of time that it might happen","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tell ahead of time that it might happen$q$, $q$Predict means "say before," and the passage says the signs help them know when an eruption might happen so towns can prepare. Explaining it afterward would not happen "before," and nothing says they can stop it.$q$, 'draft', '17773410-8578-588b-a135-7ef47bcf2369')
